{"type":"message","id":"71930f21","parentId":"4e33706f","timestamp":"2026-05-01T03:33:24.334Z","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Sender (untrusted metadata):\n```json\n{\n  \"label\": \"ClawX (gateway-client)\",\n  \"id\": \"gateway-client\",\n  \"name\": \"ClawX\",\n  \"username\": \"ClawX\"\n}\n```\n\n[Fri 2026-05-01 11:33 GMT+8] 我在启动Claude code的时候出现了这个\nMicrosoft Windows [版本 10.0.26200.8246]\n(c) Microsoft Corporation。保留所有权利。\n\nC:\\Users\\zhang>Claude\nBun is a fast JavaScript runtime, package manager, bundler, and test runner. (1.3.14+0a466a11e)\n\nUsage: bun <command> [...flags] [...args]\n\nCommands:\n run ./my-script.ts Execute a file with Bun\n lint Run a package.json script\n test Run unit tests with Bun\n x vite Execute a package binary (CLI), installing if needed (bunx)\n repl Start a REPL session with Bun\n exec Run a shell script directly with Bun\n\n install Install dependencies for a package.json (bun i)\n add hono Add a dependency to package.json (bun a)\n remove @parcel/core Remove a dependency from package.json (bun rm)\n update react Update outdated dependencies\n audit Check installed packages for vulnerabilities\n outdated Display latest versions of outdated dependencies\n link [<package>] Register or link a local npm package\n unlink Unregister a local npm package\n publish Publish a package to the npm registry\n patch <pkg> Prepare a package for patching\n pm <subcommand> Additional package management utilities\n info lyra Display package metadata from the registry\n why @remix-run/dev Explain why a package is installed\n\n build ./a.ts ./b.jsx Bundle TypeScript & JavaScript into a single file\n\n init Start an empty Bun project from a built-in template\n create elysia Create a new project from a template (bun c)\n upgrade Upgrade to latest version of Bun.\n feedback ./file1 ./file2 Provide feedback to the Bun team.\n\n <command> --help Print help text for command.\n\nLearn more about Bun: https://bun.com/docs\nJoin our Discord community: https://bun.com/discord\n\nC:\\Users\\zhang>"}],"timestamp":1777606404127}}
{"type":"message","id":"c34ac335","parentId":"71930f21","timestamp":"2026-05-01T03:33:37.482Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The user is trying to run `claude` (Claude Code) in their command prompt, but it's executing Bun instead. This is a classic PATH conflict issue — there's likely a `claude` executable that's actually a Bun executable, or the `claude` command is resolving to the Bun runtime.\n\nLet me think about this more carefully. The user typed `Claude` (with capital C) and got the Bun usage output. This means there's a `Claude` (or `claude`) command that's actually Bun.\n\nCommon causes:\n1. There's a `claude.exe` (or `claude.bat`/`claude.cmd`) in PATH that's actually a Bun wrapper/executable\n2. The Node.js/npm global install of `@anthropic-ai/claude-code` might be conflicting\n3. The bun executable might be aliased or there's a conflicting executable\n\nLet me help diagnose this. I should check what `claude` is resolving to on their system.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"Looking at this, when you type `Claude` (or `claude`), Windows is resolving it to Bun instead of Claude Code. This is likely a PATH conflict — there's probably a `claude` script/executable that's actually Bun.\n\nLet me diagnose:"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_00_gCP9AGgoJZnAbatsNDqSUuzs","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"where claude 2>&1; where Claude 2>&1","timeout":10}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"custom-customad","model":"deepseek-v4-pro","usage":{"input":36907,"output":557,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":37464,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1777606404337,"responseId":"7cc4527a-6730-455e-9c29-20fb3cb95d35"}}
