{"type":"message","id":"fd3f18fc","parentId":"84907090","timestamp":"2026-05-01T03:34:10.721Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"So the `claude.exe` exists at `C:\\Users\\zhang\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm\\node_modules\\@anthropic-ai\\claude-code\\bin\\claude.exe` and it's about 254MB (which is basically just the Bun runtime binary renamed as `claude.exe`). \n\nWhen you run `claude`, it should execute this `claude.exe`, which is Bun bundled with the Claude Code script. But instead it's showing the generic Bun help page, which means Bun is starting but not finding its bundled script.\n\nThis typically happens when:\n1. The installation is corrupted/incomplete\n2. The bun binary can't find its bundled code\n3. There's a conflict with another Bun installation\n\nLet me check if there's also a standalone Bun installation on the system that might be conflicting.\n\nActually wait - looking at the output again, when you type `Claude` (Windows is case-insensitive), it finds `claude.cmd` which calls `claude.exe`. The `claude.exe` is Bun + the Claude Code script bundled together. When Bun starts, it should run the bundled Claude Code. But instead it's showing Bun's help, which means the self-contained executable isn't working properly.\n\nLet me check:\n1. If Bun is installed separately\n2. The version of the claude package\n3. If there's a PATH conflict with another Bun","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"The exe exists (254MB — that's Bun + Claude Code bundled). But when run, Bun shows its generic help instead of starting Claude Code. Let's check a few things:"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_00_89m1eRQJSyUclUM0p3lIuFwJ","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"where bun 2>&1; Get-Command bun -ErrorAction SilentlyContinue | Select-Object Source","timeout":10}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"custom-customad","model":"deepseek-v4-pro","usage":{"input":52,"output":704,"cacheRead":38016,"cacheWrite":0,"totalToke