{"type":"message","id":"ba46723c","parentId":"33013292","timestamp":"2026-05-01T03:34:18.921Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"No separate Bun installation on PATH — so the `claude.exe` IS the Bun runtime. The issue is that Bun is starting but not finding its bundled Claude Code script.\n\nLet me try running the claude executable directly with some flags or check if it needs a specific subcommand.\n\nActually, this is a known issue. The `@anthropic-ai/claude-code` npm package bundles a `claude.exe` which is actually a Bun standalone executable. When run, Bun should detect that it's been packaged with code and execute it. If it shows the generic Bun help instead, it means the bundling is broken.\n\nLet me check the npm package version and try reinstalling.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_00_s9pKwaJXoXlaaJ9BJK5VVChD","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"npm list -g @anthropic-ai/claude-code 2>&1","timeout":15}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"custom-customad","model":"deepseek-v4-pro","usage":{"input":98,"output":353,"cacheRead":38400,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":38851,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1777606451189,"responseId":"fcaa4bb1-4393-4b38-94c2-5cd63545cea8"}}
