{"type":"message","id":"1ae85297","parentId":"9dd27a73","timestamp":"2026-05-01T03:34:38.210Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Only `claude.exe` in the bin directory. This is the self-contained Bun binary. Let me check if there's a `cli.js` somewhere else, maybe in the package root.\n\nActually, the issue might be that the exe is just Bun without the Claude Code script embedded. Or maybe there's a PATH issue where another Bun executable shadows it.\n\nWait, let me re-read the user's output more carefully. They typed `Claude` (capital C). On Windows, CMD/PowerShell is case-insensitive for commands. But the output shows `Bun is a fast JavaScript runtime...` which means a Bun executable was launched.\n\nThe `claude.exe` at 254MB should be Bun + Claude Code. If Bun starts and shows its generic help, it usually means:\n1. The embedded script isn't being found\n2. The binary is corrupted\n3. Something is intercepting the call\n\nLet me try running the exe directly with full path:","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_00_ZKbSTO6zS45Sp1rZnNyrVqWN","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"& \"C:\\Users\\zhang\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm\\node_modules\\@anthropic-ai\\claude-code\\bin\\claude.exe\" --version 2>&1","timeout":15}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"custom-customad","model":"deepseek-v4-pro","usage":{"input":88,"output":502,"cacheRead":38912,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":39502,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1777606467950,"responseId":"ee3287a4-abd3-4a2b-b564-b851a7126f11"}}
