{"type":"message","id":"fae74175","parentId":"3a896932","timestamp":"2026-05-01T03:34:56.288Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"So `claude.exe --version` returns `1.3.14`, which is the Bun version. That confirms that `claude.exe` is starting as Bun but not running Claude Code. This is a broken installation — the Bun standalone executable isn't finding its embedded code.\n\nLet me try reinstalling Claude Code. The typical fix is:\n\n```\nnpm uninstall -g @anthropic-ai/claude-code\nnpm install -g @anthropic-ai/claude-code\n```\n\nBut first, let me check if there's a newer version or if there's some known issue.\n\nActually, wait — let me also check the file metadata to see if it's actually a Bun standalone binary that's been properly compiled. Let me look at the file size and maybe try running it with `--help` to see what Bun commands are embedded.\n\nActually, I already know the fix for this. The `claude.exe` is a Bun standalone binary that embeds the Claude Code TypeScript source. When you run `claude`, Bun is supposed to detect it was compiled with `bun build --compile` and run the embedded code. If it shows the generic Bun help instead, something went wrong with the compilation or the binary is corrupted.\n\nThe fix is to reinstall:\n\n```\nnpm uninstall -g @anthropic-ai/claude-code\nnpm install -g @anthropic-ai/claude-code\n```\n\nOr use the Bun-based approach if they have Bun installed:\n```\nbun add -g @anthropic-ai/claude-code\n```\n\nActually, let me also check if this is a known issue. Let me search for it.\n\nActually, let me just suggest the reinstall. But first, let me also check if there's a Node.js version that could work as a fallback.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"Now I see the problem clearly. When you run `claude`, the `claude.exe` is supposed to be a **self-contained Bun binary** with Claude Code embedded inside. But it's only showing Bun's generic help — meaning the embedded Claude Code script isn't being detected. Bun version 1.3.14 is starting, but not the bundled app.\n\nThis is a **corrupted/broken installation**. The fix is to reinstall:"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_00_jqLbtFITY838BZRfXGWPOCjG","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"npm uninstall -g @anthropic-ai/claude-code 2>&1","timeout":30}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"custom-customad","model":"deepseek-v4-pro","usage":{"input":22,"output":902,"cacheRead":39296,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":40220,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1777606478523,"responseId":"bba76705-cd60-4aa6-98bf-25332aaafdf2"}}
